// NEW fields to add to the existing InvoiceItem model:
//
//   blocked           Boolean  @default(false)
//   blockedByRuleId   String?
//   blockedByRuleName String?
//
// Semantics:
//   - blocked: true if this item matched an active rule AT SAVE TIME.
//     Never re-evaluated after save (task requirement: "changing a
//     rule later does not re-evaluate invoices already saved").
//   - blockedByRuleId: kept for analytics/audit only (e.g. "which
//     rule causes the most blocks"). It is a nullable, non-cascading
//     reference — if the rule is later deleted, this can become an
//     orphaned id or be set to null; either way it must NEVER be used
//     to look up display text at read time.
//   - blockedByRuleName: the actual snapshot used for display. Copied
//     from ProductRule.name at the moment of evaluation. This is what
//     makes the warning survive the rule being renamed or deleted, as
//     required by the task.
//
// If InvoiceItem.blockedByRuleId references ProductRule, the relation
// must be optional and use onDelete: SetNull (or no defined relation
// at the Prisma level at all, just a plain unindexed string column) —
// NOT onDelete: Cascade or Restrict, since deleting a rule must not
// delete or block deletion of historical invoice items.
//
// Example relation if a typed FK is preferred:
//   blockedByRule ProductRule? @relation(fields: [blockedByRuleId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)
